1 line: Each slash below divides. Read as a regex, the slash would run up to the comment and hide it.
4 trailing line: after a name
5 trailing line: after a number
6 trailing line: after a hex number
7 trailing line: after a number with no integer part
8 trailing line: after a property
9 trailing line: after a parenthesis
10 trailing line: after a bracket
11 trailing line: after a postfix increment
12 trailing line: after a postfix decrement
14 trailing line: after a line break, which ends no statement before a slash
16 trailing line: a / b / g, three names and two divisions
17 trailing line: after an object literal in parentheses
18 trailing line: after a call whose argument is a function
19 trailing line: after a function expression
20 trailing line: after a class expression
21 trailing line: after an object literal
22 trailing line: after an object literal in a ternary
23 trailing line: after a template
24 trailing line: after a string
25 trailing line: after a regex
26 trailing line: after true
27 trailing line: after null
28 trailing line: after a property named like a keyword
29 trailing line: after optional chaining
30 trailing line: after a division assignment
38 trailing line: after this and super
